# =============================================================================
# DOCUMENTATION HEADER — Cost-Based Allocator — user prompt template
# =============================================================================
# This header is documentation for maintainers. The runtime loader reads the
# entire file (including these lines) into the LLM prompt string. Keep the
# original instructional sections below unchanged in meaning and order.
#
# SECTION: Placeholders
#   {available_tasks} (frontier) and {agent_descriptions} (incl. previous_task_id).
#
# SECTION: Constraint
#   Each agent at most one available task this round.
#
# SECTION: Response shape
#   JSON object mapping agent_id → integer task_id (no nulls/strings).
#
# =============================================================================
Given the available tasks and agents, assign each agent at most one available task.

Available Tasks: {available_tasks}
Agents: {agent_descriptions}

Respond ONLY with a JSON object mapping agent IDs to assigned integer task IDs, e.g. {{"agent_id": 5, ...}}. Do not use null, string names, or non-integer task IDs.